{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENEK3u2ftkDnhfNtH2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both bugs come from `hidden` being a DynamoDB reserved word, and it fails in two different ways. The fix aliases every attribute name in every expression, and the tests now catch the silent case. Tests pass (10 of 10), and the write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed or deployed.\n\n**The causes**\n\n- **Prod crash:** `hide()` used `SET hidden = :h` with a bare name in an UpdateExpression. DynamoDB rejects that with a ValidationException, so the handler returned 500. This matches `logs/prod-error.log`.\n- **Staging feed (silent):** `feed()` listed `hidden` bare in a ProjectionExpression. DynamoDB drops that attribute from the result without an error, so `not i.get(\"hidden\")` never saw it and nothing was filtered out. The hand-hidden item is correct in the table, since the CLI used an alias. The feed is not cached and reads the same table; its projection was the problem.\n- **Latent:** `archive()` used bare `status` in a ConditionExpression. It isn't wired to the API yet, so it hasn't broken anything, but it would fail the same way.\n\n**The fix**\n\n- `src/app.py`: every name in every expression is now an alias (`#hidden`, `#slug`, `#status`, …), including names I don't know to be reserved. The rule is blanket, so future field names are covered too.\n- `tests/fake_dynamo.py`: `FakeTable` now raises on a bare reserved word in a projection by default. The real service is silent there, which is why the bug was hard to see. `strict_projection=False` reproduces the real behaviour.\n- `tests/test_feed.py`: five new tests cover `hide()` (flag written, unknown slug rejected, hidden story leaves the feed, others stay), `archive()`, and the strict-projection guard. The hidden-story test sets the flag on the record the feed reads. All five failed before the fix.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- The fake's reserved-word list is a subset of the real one, so the tests can't prove a name is safe. The alias-everything rule is the real protection; the tests only check that aliases are used.\n- Nothing was deployed. Staging's feed and prod's Hide should be re-checked after a deploy."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2287,"cache_read_input_tokens":42931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2287},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77beed2d-7cf8-4dc2-8e30-726d10578f04","uuid":"5ec32abb-2ffe-46e5-b8f0-4e44a7ecee9d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:36:05.104Z","request_id":"req_011CgENEJhK69FLcqRQ4W5S1"}
